  Verification timings, wall-clock:

   n          BLS verify    BLS decode    Ed25519 batch verify
  ━━━━━━━━━  ━━━━━━━━━━━━  ━━━━━━━━━━━━  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
   1,000      936.653 ms    107.726 ms               17.140 ms
  ─────────  ────────────  ────────────  ──────────────────────
   10,000        9.553 s       1.082 s              162.425 ms
  ─────────  ────────────  ────────────  ──────────────────────
   100,000      93.048 s      10.721 s                 1.577 s

  The BLS path is much slower on receiver CPU in this benchmark, not faster. The compression result does show a real signature-byte win, but on this proxy corpus it’s not enough to justify a CPU-savings story. The honest
  motivation is bandwidth-only, and it needs to say that plainly.

